it does mark the unofficial start to  summer so  uh in that regard registered dietitian  mia sin shares a nutritious alfresco  dining menu to enjoy  outdoors as the weather heats up not  quite barbecue  hey las vegas now happy unofficial start  to summer i have the ultimate better for  you all fresco dining menu that's easy  to make  and nutritious starting with appetizers  these mozzarella bites and sweet onion  petals by farmridge are ready in minutes  simply pop these mozzarella bites in the  microwave for 50 seconds or in the oven  for a melt-in-your-mouth appetizer made  with 100  real mozzarella cheese so they're a good  source of protein and calcium  these crispy sweet onion petals make a  great burger topping and  are ready to eat after 10 minutes in the  oven they also come with an  aussie style dipping sauce buy them in  the freezer aisle of albertson's bonds  walmart and more just check the product  locator at farmridge.com  now another easy appetizer that can help  you meet your recommended  three plus servings of veggies for the  day is my veggie dip cups  i paired sliced veggies with the new  creamy fresh cravings hummus which  offers a balanced mix of good fats fiber  and plant protein from chilean extra  virgin olive oil non-gmo chickpeas  and savory tahini it comes in different  flavors including classic and roasted  red bell pepper  another nutritious dip to pair with  sliced veggies and tortilla chips  is my single serve seven layer dip start  with beans and top with guacamole  sour cream or plain greek yogurt fresh  cravings refrigerated salsa  cheese and green onion salsa is  classified as a veggie by the usda  and like the fresh cravings hummus the  refrigerated salsa is made with a short  list of whole food ingredients  find both the fresh cravings salsa and  hummus in the produce section at smith's  next an all fresco dining menu is  incomplete without burgers  these new cauliflower veggie burgers by  dr prager's are packed with six  different vegetables and feature the  same veggie forward look and flavor  profile that dr praker's customers know  and love  dr prager's products make it easy and  convenient for the whole family to enjoy  vegetable packed meals made with clean  nourishing ingredients  find them at whole foods nationwide in  the freezer section  then finally i have a festive dessert  with benefits made with only four  ingredients  these oat cups are packed with filling  fiber and are naturally sweetened with  fruit to a large mixing bowl combine two  cups of quick oats and two large ripe  bananas press the mixture into a  pre-greased muffin pan and bake for 10  minutes at 350 degrees fahrenheit or  until set  fill your oat cups with plain or vanilla  yogurt and top with berries  i hope you enjoyed all of these recipes  and tips you can find them at my website  nutritionbymia.com  and nutritionbymia on instagram where i  also share meal ideas  and nutrition tips daily
 

